WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our next guest is a talente
actress and comedian

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.603
you know from her work as
Meredith on "The Office."

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:07.073
Every episode of "The Office
is now streaming on Peacock.

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:10.243
Please welcome to the show
our friend Kate Flannery.

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:11.277 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Hi, Kate!

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:12.846 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Hey, Seth! How are ya?

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:15.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm good.
I'm always so happy to see you

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:19.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
Kate, I knew your history
as an improviser in Chicago.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:22.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did not know
you were from Philly.

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:25.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that someplace
you get back to often?

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:26.593 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I do.

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:28.128 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I'm one of seven kids,

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:31.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
and my dad is --
he's still kickin'.

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:33.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's the best.
He's in his 90s.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:34.467 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He's hilarious.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:37.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, yeah, I try to get home
as much as I can.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.838 line:92%
I was just home in October

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:41.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got to, like, quarantine
for two weeks

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:43.843 line:92%
in my friend's garage apartmen

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:44.978 line:92%
and then spend time with my dad.

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:47.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I kind of felt like Fonzi
for a few weeks.

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:49.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
You got the Fonzie life.

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:50.617 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-I did. It was awesome.

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:53.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You mentioned
you're one of seven.

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.888 line:92%
You're the youngest of seven

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:56.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that right?
-I am.

00:00:56.156 --> 00:00:57.757 line:92%
I have a fraternal twin sister

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:59.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
but technically,
I'm the youngest.

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:00.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
-Damn it. [ Chuckles ]

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:04.264
-And now, do you feel like
being the youngest of seven,

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:06.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
can you track back
in your life's journey

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:10.270 size:88% position:44%
that that maybe is why
you're in show business?

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.205 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Absolutely. 300%.

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:13.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I don't know why
I even bother

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:18.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
to spend money on a therapist,
it's so stereotypical.

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:21.314 line:92%
-You were a Chicago improviser

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:25.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
Those must have been formative
and exciting years for you

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:26.920 line:92%
-The greatest. The greatest.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.421 line:92%
I mean, you know, it's funny

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:30.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
I work a lot
with Jane Lynch now.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:31.891 line:92%
We do a live show together

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:33.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we did a Christmas album
together.

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:34.294 line:92%
But I realized, I figured ou

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:37.263
the very, very first time
I ever went to Second City

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:40.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
Jane Lynch was onstage
understudying for Bonnie Hun

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause it was
Bonnie Hunt's wedding day.

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:44.237 line:92%
And then Bonnie Hunt came back

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:48.341 size:75% position:38%
to do the improv set
in her wedding gown.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.877 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:51.644 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's pretty good.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:53.246 size:84% position:42%
I don't think my wife
would have been psyched

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:56.883
on our wedding night if I told
her I was off to do some improv.

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:59.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think that's why
she's divorced now.

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:01.321 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:03.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They say you can usually
see the signs.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.358 line:92%
You can usually see the signs.

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:07.560 line:92%
-You can't take off one night?

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
One night?
You can't miss one show?!

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I -- It's amazing
you said that.

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.032 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
The first time --

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:14.934 size:81% position:41%
One of the first times
I went to Second City,

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
I saw Tina Fey understudying
for John Glaser.

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:20.740
And it is -- I mean, when yo
look back at how lucky we were

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:23.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was crazy
who you would just see

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:26.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
that then over the course
of the following two decades

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:29.315
has been exactly as successful
as you kind of hoped they'd be

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.151 line:92%
when you first saw them onstage.

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:32.552 line:92%
-Absolutely. No, it's amazing.

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:34.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, like, I also remembe
when I was there,

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:37.357
John Favreau could not get hired
at Second City.

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:38.658 size:88% position:44% line:92%
He was literally a host.

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:40.326 size:81% position:41% line:92%
He was seating people.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:41.394 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:43.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's -- It's a shame
it didn't work out for him

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:45.798 line:92%
-Too bad. That's a shame.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:50.036 size:84% position:42%
-So, "The Office" now
is not just on Peacock,

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:53.573 size:81% position:41%
but also sort of these
extra long episodes,

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:55.742 line:92%
which are really fun for people.

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:57.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel a growing number
of people

00:02:57.577 --> 00:03:00.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
who continue to become fan
of the show every day.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
What was your audition process
for "The Office" like?

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, initially, I auditioned
for the part of Jan,

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:09.489
who's Michael's boss, played b
the beautiful Melora Hardin.

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:12.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
Clearly, they went
in a different way.

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:15.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I actually was not
in the pilot.

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:16.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I ended up replacing
somebody,

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:17.564 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and they kind of did...

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:19.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know, I think they wer
trying to figure out

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.067 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
who everybody was.

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.535 line:92%
So I'm not even sure who..

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:23.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wasn't even sure
that Meredith --

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:25.672 size:78% position:39%
I mean, I had no idea
she was gonna become

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:27.674 size:75% position:38% line:92%
a drunk or a floozy.

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:30.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know,
my dad owns a bar.

00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:32.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, my dad owned
Flannery's Tavern for years,

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:34.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I feel like,
playing an alcoholic,

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:37.050 line:92%
I come by it quite honestly.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.384 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's really, um...

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:41.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
Don't take this the wrong way.
It seems really cliché

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:46.226
to be a Flannery whose dad owned
a bar called Flannery's Tavern

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:48.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know. I know.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:48.728 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You know what?

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:51.464
Irish people, we don't get upset
about that stuff.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:52.432 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We just don't.

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:54.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I mean, Seth,
I always say,

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:56.402 line:92%
if you can't type, stereotype.

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
Right?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.537 --> 00:03:59.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it's like,
this is who we -- I --

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:03.509
Why not be loud and proud
of who I am, you know?

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:08.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, you mentioned
you didn't know

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:10.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
what the character was gonna
develop into.

00:04:10.617 --> 00:04:11.951 line:92%
Like, what was the process like?

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:15.788
Did it sort of very slowly
reveal itself over time?

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:18.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Did writers tell new advance?

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:19.525 line:92%
-Nobody told me in advance

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:22.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I do remember the firs
Halloween episode

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:25.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
during season two,
that's when I had

00:04:25.198 --> 00:04:27.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
my first monologue
about being an alcoholic.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.135 line:92%
And I guess it was so dark

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:32.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the network decided
not to use it.

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:33.306 line:92%
So we had to wait till Christmas

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:35.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
to reveal that Meredith
was a drunk.

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:37.176 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:37.877 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-I think we all -- Yeah.

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:40.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, by Christmas,
there's no secrets anymore

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:43.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right? I mean...
-Meredith ended up --

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:44.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
you wouldn't have probably
guessed this

00:04:44.384 --> 00:04:45.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
from our first
introduction to her --

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:49.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
a fair amount of stunts
over the years.

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:49.589 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes!

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:50.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you participate
in the stunts?

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:54.494 size:81% position:41%
What was your level of
engagement with those?

00:04:54.494 --> 00:04:57.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did most of my own stunts
on the show.

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:58.498 line:92%
I actually kind of loved it.

00:04:58.498 --> 00:05:00.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just remember
the first season, like,

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:03.803
Greg Daniels had asked me
to dress up like Madonna

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:05.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they were just doing
a still picture

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:08.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Rainn Wilson
and Steve Carell

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:10.910 size:81% position:41% line:92%
as Crockett and Tubbs.

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:13.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I was like,
"Yeah, I'll be Madonna."

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:16.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, anything -- I was just
up for almost anything.

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:18.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did not set my hair on fir
in the Christmas episode,

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:21.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Moroccan Christmas."
And I didn't shave my head

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:22.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the lice episode
the last season.

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:24.057 size:75% position:38%
But other than that,
I've done every...

00:05:24.057 --> 00:05:26.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got hit by the car,
I had the bat on the head,

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:27.393 line:92%
the bag and the -- you know.

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:30.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I -- everything.
Did it all.

00:05:30.096 --> 00:05:31.097 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-What's the prep like

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:33.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you're, you know, somebod
with an improv background

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:35.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
about to be hit by a car
on a comedy show?

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:40.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] Well, there wa
a safety meeting.

00:05:40.273 --> 00:05:42.909
And Greg Daniels was tryin
to get me all, like, loose

00:05:42.909 --> 00:05:45.778
We were doing jumping jacks.
And I just had to kind of roll

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:51.084
onto the grass and then roll
off the car onto a giant mat

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:53.119 line:92%
[ Laughing ] That was it.

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:56.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I literally think the
editor, Dave Rogers,

00:05:56.055 --> 00:05:58.458 size:84% position:42%
pushed me a little bit
right before we started

00:05:58.458 --> 00:05:59.792 line:92%
just to give me the momentum

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:01.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it was a team effort.
-Nice crew.

00:06:01.194 --> 00:06:03.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did not do this by --
I cannot take credit by myself

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:07.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It takes a village to get hit
by a car on "The Office."

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:09.068 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:11.738
-Back in your Chicago improv
days, which would make sense -

00:06:11.738 --> 00:06:15.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was when SNL was going an
finding people to audition

00:06:15.074 --> 00:06:16.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
so you actually auditioned
for SNL

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:18.778 line:92%
I guess in the '90s, right

00:06:18.778 --> 00:06:19.579 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Yeah, I was up for SNL.

00:06:19.579 --> 00:06:23.249
Lorne Michaels came to a sho
I did at the Annoyance Theatre

00:06:23.249 --> 00:06:24.417 line:92%
I was also at Second City,

00:06:24.417 --> 00:06:26.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I did another show
at the Annoyance.

00:06:26.386 --> 00:06:28.588 line:92%
And he brought his good budd

00:06:28.588 --> 00:06:31.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
Quincy Jones, as you do.
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:33.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sitting in these crappy
folding chairs.

00:06:33.326 --> 00:06:35.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think we had to do
the show on a Tuesday night.

00:06:35.728 --> 00:06:38.030
They had to move the show
because he was coming.

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:39.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we had lunch
the next day.

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:44.337
And he also was looking at three
other women from the show.

00:06:44.337 --> 00:06:47.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, Mike Shoemaker,
your producer,

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:49.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
was with Lorne at the time
'cause he used to work on SNL.

00:06:49.876 --> 00:06:55.047
And so, the process was that you
would walk to lunch with Lorne

00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:57.650
and then have lunch, and the
switch and be with Michael

00:06:57.650 --> 00:06:59.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
or the opposite.
So you'd always have somebod

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:02.488
to be -- like, let them have a
private conversation close by,

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:03.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
if that makes any sense?
-Yeah.

00:07:03.589 --> 00:07:07.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it doesn't make sense,
but Lorne would do that.

00:07:07.126 --> 00:07:08.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:07:08.928 --> 00:07:10.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
and the thing is, like,

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:12.765
I'm friends with the other women
that's being considered.

00:07:12.765 --> 00:07:14.700
It was Melanie Hutsell, an
she ended up getting the job

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:17.103 size:81% position:41%
And like, of course,
I'm, like, so Catholic

00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:18.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I kind of didn't know
what to do.

00:07:18.237 --> 00:07:20.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, like, you don't want
to be a douche bag.

00:07:20.173 --> 00:07:21.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
You want to be happy
for your friends.

00:07:21.941 --> 00:07:25.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know, thousands
of dollars of therapy later,

00:07:25.645 --> 00:07:27.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
you go, "Okay,
I guess I had a right

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:29.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be a little bummed
about that. That's okay."

00:07:29.148 --> 00:07:31.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, of course.
-That's alright.

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:35.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I think all of us
are so happy

00:07:35.488 --> 00:07:37.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
that it worked out
the way it did.

00:07:37.323 --> 00:07:40.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is such a delight to go bac
and watch that show

00:07:40.793 --> 00:07:43.930
that is just -- it not onl
maintained its excellence,

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:46.466 size:81% position:41%
it just holds so well.
It just keeps so well.

00:07:46.466 --> 00:07:47.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you're such a big
part of it.

00:07:47.733 --> 00:07:48.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thanks so much
for being here, Kate.

00:07:48.801 --> 00:07:50.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much, Seth.
You're the best.

